!MesaLibs - riscos-mesa's shared libraries
==========================================

Programs built as "mixed" programs with the riscos-mesa devkit (UnixLib
linked into the program, the other libraries shared) load OpenGL (OSMesa),
EGL, GLU, GLUT, SDL 2 and OpenAL from here, through !SharedLibs. Programs
that use them share one copy of each library in memory.

Install: copy !MesaLibs into !Boot.Resources (open !Boot, then Resources).
Programs that need it boot it when they start. It sets MesaLibs$Path and
runs DAClamp, which lifts RISC OS 5's 128 MB limit on dynamic areas given a
maximum size (OS_DynamicArea 8,0,-1,0, as !GTKLibs does). !SharedLibs puts
every shared library in one such area, sized when the first program loads
one, so the limit has to go before then: keep !MesaLibs in !Boot.Resources.

Also needed:
- !SharedLibs, also in !Boot.Resources (PackMan's SharedLibs package, or
  the one Iris includes);
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, and ARMEABISupport.

Mixed programs need !SharedLibs' ld-riscos/so/2 loader and SOManager 3.x,
which PackMan's SharedLibs 4.0 lacks: they are in SharedLibs here, and
each time !MesaLibs is booted it copies them into !SharedLibs where they
are missing (SOManager also where the one there is older), as !GTKLibs
does. Nothing else in !SharedLibs is touched. Restart after installing,
so the newer SOManager is the one loaded. The loader's licence is
SharedLibs.COPYRIGHT-ld; SOManager 3.04 is GCCSDK's (Lee Noar).

The libraries (in lib):
  libOSMesa/so/8    OpenGL 2.1 and OpenGL ES 1.1/2.0 (Mesa 20.3.5)
  libEGL/so/1       EGL for RISC OS
  libGLU/so/1       GLU 9.0.1
  libglut/so/3      freeglut 3.8.0
  libSDL2-2.0/so/0  SDL 2.32.10
  libopenal/so/1    OpenAL Soft 1.19.1
  libMesaGPU/so/1   Mesa 26.1.6's driver for a Pi 4's GPU, for programs
                    linked with -lMesaGPU. Other programs never load it.

GPUProbe says what the GPU gives programs here (for RISC3D's setup window,
or *Obey <MesaLibs$Dir>.GPUProbe -o <file> from a task window): for OpenGL,
OpenGL ES (its highest) and OpenGL ES 1.1, lines of "key: value" --
gpuprobe (the format, 1), egl, then for each: api, route (RISC3D,
software or none), version, renderer, shading, max_texture_size,
extensions, end.

Programs don't choose between the GPU and software: RISC3D decides. With
!RISC3D in !Boot.Resources, programs draw on the GPU driver it loads at
start-up; without one they draw in software. LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE or
RISC3D$Disable (system variables) keep everything in software.

Programs that link the devkit's static libraries (as before) don't need
this. https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-mesa - licences in LICENCES.txt
there (and in Licences here): Mesa 20.3.5 and 26.1.6 (MIT), GLU (SGI B 2.0), freeglut (MIT/X), SDL (zlib), OpenAL
Soft (LGPL 2 or later: being a shared library, it can be replaced).
